# =============================================================================
# PPC Service — Environment Variables (local dev)
# Copy to .env.local and fill in credentials. .env.local is gitignored.
# The Makefile does `include .env.local; export`, so these override config.yaml
# via Viper's env binding. NOT used in Kubernetes — staging/prod inject config
# via K8s Secrets + ConfigMaps (see goapps-infra). This file is LOCAL ONLY.
# =============================================================================

# --- App ---
APP_ENV=development                 # development | staging | production
LOG_LEVEL=debug                     # debug | info | warn | error

# --- PPC Postgres (docker-compose ppc-postgres, port 5436) ---
# config.yaml defaults already match these; uncomment only to override.
# PPC_DATABASE_HOST=localhost
# PPC_DATABASE_PORT=5436
# PPC_DATABASE_USER=ppc
# PPC_DATABASE_PASSWORD=ppc123
# PPC_DATABASE_NAME=ppc_db

# =============================================================================
# --- Oracle (R&D / staging) — READ-ONLY. NEVER writes to Oracle. ---
# =============================================================================
# IMPORTANT: The PPC Go code opens ONE Oracle connection as a SINGLE user, and
# reads across MULTIPLE schemas via that user's SELECT grants. It does NOT use
# per-schema connections (unlike a Laravel multi-connection setup). So you supply
# exactly ONE username/password below — pick the user that has SELECT on all the
# schemas/objects listed under "Schemas the code reads".
#
# go-ora connects with host + port + service (SID/service name) + user + password.
ORACLE_HOST=                        # e.g. mgtoradb-scan.mutugading.com  (R&D host)
ORACLE_PORT=1521
ORACLE_SERVICE=                     # Oracle service name / SID (e.g. althara)
ORACLE_USER=                        # single connecting user (e.g. mgtdat)
ORACLE_PASSWORD=
# Optional pool tuning (config.yaml defaults: 5 conns / 10m lifetime)
# ORACLE_MAX_OPEN_CONNS=5
# ORACLE_CONN_MAX_LIFETIME=10m
#
# --- Schemas the code reads (this ONE user needs SELECT grants on all): ---
#   MGTDAT.PPC_TXT_PRODUCTION      (TXT/TWT production ETL — txt_production_source.go)
#   MGTDAT.PPC_SPG_PRODUCTION      (SPG production ETL      — spg_production_source.go)
#   MGTDAT.PPC_GRADE_ACTUAL        (packing grade ETL       — grade_actual_source.go)
#   MGTDAT.MGT_SO_PENDING_WEB      (sales-order staging ETL — so_pending_source.go)
#   ASPTXT.TXTMACH                 (machine sync            — machine_source.go)
# The MGTDAT.PPC_* summary tables are populated INSIDE Oracle by the stored
# procedures in docs-markdown/.../oracle/PPC_ORACLE_PROCEDURES.sql (which read the
# raw ASPTXT/ASPSPG/ASPAK/ASMAR tables). The Go ETL only reads the digested
# MGTDAT summaries + ASPTXT.TXTMACH — it never touches the raw source schemas.
#
# If you connect as MGTDAT and lack a grant on ASPTXT.TXTMACH, the machine sync
# will degrade (finance-only, area empty). Ensure: GRANT SELECT ON ASPTXT.TXTMACH
# TO MGTDAT;  (or connect as a user that already has it).

# =============================================================================
# --- Finance internal service token (PPC BFF/service → finance master reads) ---
# =============================================================================
# MUST equal finance's jwt.service_secret. Finance accepts x-service-secret OR
# x-internal-token. Overrides finance_client.internal_service_token in config.yaml.
PPC_FINANCE_INTERNAL_TOKEN=dev-service-secret-change-in-production
# IAM internal token (PPC → IAM notifications). Must equal IAM security token.
# PPC_IAM_INTERNAL_TOKEN=dev-internal-token-2026

# --- Finance / IAM gRPC endpoints (config.yaml defaults usually fine locally) ---
# FINANCE_GRPC_HOST=localhost
# FINANCE_GRPC_PORT=50051
# IAM_GRPC_HOST=localhost
# IAM_GRPC_PORT=50052
